codex
The reference run is healthy: 9.3M trainable parameters, all 15,576 questions represented, and loss has settled from ~10 to roughly 0.6–1.0. Corpus profiling also exposes a likely transfer mismatch: half the score is knowledge, yet the fixed training set has no MMLU-style knowledge source; the architecture must preserve and expose pretrained knowledge rather than learn it from labels. I’ll use that criterion when selecting the first modification.
