+# Small-model decision research log
+
+## Fixed setup
+
+- Base: Qwen2.5-0.5B at revision `060db6499f32faf8b98477b0a26969ef7d8b9987`.
+- Train: decision-v7, 12,576 records / 15,576 questions.
+- Public development: 1,156 single-question records; 1,046 scored and 110 evidence-removed diagnostics.
+- Metric: half knowledge (MMLU and MMLU-Pro source means), half equal-weighted non-knowledge source means.
+
+## Corpus observations
+
+- Training sources: 10 public classification sources with 1,000 records each, 896 legacy-policy records, and 1,680 compositional records.
+- No training source is a knowledge multiple-choice benchmark. Retaining and exposing base-model knowledge is therefore essential rather than merely fitting the decision corpus.
+- Choice cardinality ranges from 2 to 77. Banking77 (77 choices) is also the longest common train input (mean 738 tokens), while public MMLU-Pro has about 10 choices and reaches 738 tokens.
+- The reference option endpoint is causal and can see earlier options; the random pointer head combines each endpoint with one shared decision state. This creates order-dependent representations and asks a randomly initialized head to rediscover how to expose pretrained knowledge.
+
+## Experiment 0: reference
+
+Command: `/opt/kev-venv/bin/python /workspace/candidate/train.py`
+
+Configuration: two epochs, global batch 8, LoRA rank 16 on all attention and MLP projections, random 256-wide pointer head, OneCycle peak LR 1e-4, random fixed delimiter embeddings, ordinary cross-entropy.
+
+Pre-registered hypotheses for follow-up:
+
+1. A permutation-equivariant option scorer over option-isolated representations should improve transfer and remove causal option-order artifacts.
+2. A pretrained yes/no verbalizer direction or a zero-initialized residual scorer should expose base knowledge more directly than a fully random bilinear pointer.
+3. Restricting backbone adaptation and using a separate faster head LR should reduce knowledge forgetting while retaining task-format learning.
+4. Ordinal RPS and permutation consistency are secondary candidates after an architecture comparison.
+
+Status: training in progress.
